  ],
  "text": "Move a magnet near a wire and electricity appears. Run electricity through a wire and a magnet appears. They were studied as two separate things for a very long time. Faraday showed that it is one relationship read in two directions. Which means a motor and a generator are the same machine. Feed it electricity and the shaft turns. Turn the shaft and electricity comes out. Which is why almost every power station on Earth is doing the same final thing. Coal, gas and nuclear all boil water. The steam pushes a turbine. The turbine spins a magnet. Hydro and wind skip the boiling and push the same wheel directly. Solar is the odd one out. It has no moving part at all, and no spinning magnet anywhere. Almost all the electricity you have ever used came from something turning a magnet round. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
